   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Three distances",
   "texto": [
    "The Japanese distinguishes three distances, as does the Spanish. **これ** = this (near me). **それ** = that (near you). **あれ** = that (far from both).",
    "These three words go **solas**. If they go in front of a name, they change to **この**, **その**, **あの**: **この ほん** (this book), **あの ひと** (that person)."
   ]
  },
